@page 58 morning-prayer
c __MORNING PRAYER.__
  The Forgiveness of sins; The Resurrection of
  the body, And the Life everlasting. __Amen.__
R ¶ __And after that, these Prayers following, all devoutly kneeling; the__
  __Minister first pronouncing with a loud voice,__
V+50 The Lord be with you:
V+50 __Answ.__ And with thy spirit.
V+34 ¶ __Minister.__ Let us pray.
V+50 Lord, have mercy upon us.
V+59 __Christ, have mercy upon us.__
V+50 Lord, have mercy upon us.
R ¶ __Then the Minister, Clerks, and People shall say the Lord’s Prayer__
  __with a loud voice.__
I OUR Father, which art in Heaven, Hal-
  lowed be thy Name; Thy kingdom come;
  Thy will be done in earth, As it is in hea-
  ven: Give us this day our daily bread; And
  forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive them
  that trespass against us; And lead us not in-
  to temptation, But deliver us from evil. __Amen.__
R ¶ __Then the Priest standing up, shall say,__
P O Lord, shew thy mercy upon us;
P __Answ.__ And grant us thy salvation.
P __Priest.__ O Lord, save the King;
P __Answ.__ And mercifully hear us, when we
  call upon thee.
P __Priest.__ Endue thy Ministers with righteous-
  ness;
P __Answ.__ And make thy chosen people joyful.
P __Priest.__ O Lord, save thy people;
P __Answ.__ And bless thine inheritance.
f __Priest.__
